# Cloudflare API token for automated tunnel creation — OPTIONAL, separate from cloudflare.env
#
# Only needed if you use `uis network create cloudflare --env <name> --domain <domain>` to create
# the tunnel + DNS records via the Cloudflare API, instead of the dashboard (see Step 1 in
# website/docs/networking/cloudflare.md). The dashboard path needs nothing in this file.
#
# This is a DIFFERENT credential from CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN in cloudflare.env — that one lets
# cloudflared connect to an already-created tunnel; this one lets OpenTofu create the tunnel and
# its DNS records in the first place. Not interchangeable, not a wizard-written file — create it
# once, by hand, following the steps below, then save it here yourself (mode 600).
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Create the token once (dashboard > My Profile > API Tokens > Create Token > Create Custom Token,
# https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens):
#   Name: opentofu-urbalurba-tunnels
#   Permissions (3 rows):
#     1. Account | Cloudflare Tunnel | Edit
#     2. Zone    | DNS               | Edit
#     3. Zone    | Zone              | Read
#   Account Resources: Include > the account (Cloudflare Tunnel applies account-wide).
#   Zone Resources: Include > Specific zone — add each domain you'll create a tunnel for.
#     Do NOT use "All zones" — that would let this token edit DNS on every zone in the account,
#     not just the ones `uis network create cloudflare` is meant to touch.
#   No IP filtering, no TTL. Create Token.
# Cloudflare shows the token (starts "cfut_") ONCE. It cannot be read back — if you lose it,
# create a new one. Add each new domain to this token's zone list before creating its tunnel.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""
